MLX #4723 added `sdpa_split`, a Metal kernel for 2 to 8 query tokens whose stacked rows (tokens times query heads
per KV head) fall between 33 and 128. At kL >= 128 it returns results about 300x less accurate than the vector
kernels it replaced (max error against a float64 reference 3e-2 to 4e-2, against 1e-4), at head_dim 64, 96, 128,
192 and 256, causal or unmasked: ml-explore/mlx#4808. This keeps the vector kernels and the full-attention kernel
on those calls, which is what v0.32.3 ran. Drop the patch when upstream fixes the kernel.

--- a/mlx/backend/metal/scaled_dot_product_attention.cpp
+++ b/mlx/backend/metal/scaled_dot_product_attention.cpp
@@ -50,7 +50,8 @@ bool use_split(
     int window_size,
     bool output_logsumexp,
     Stream s) {
-  if (s.device != Device::gpu) {
+  // Off: sdpa_split (#4723) is ~300x less accurate than the vector kernels it replaces (ml-explore/mlx#4808).
+  if (s.device != Device::gpu || true) {
     return false;
   }
   const int D = q.shape(-1);
